  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added fail-closed final-host acceptance for all four release targets plus a complete digest-bound third-party source/license inventory. Linux artifacts must retain the exact baseline, SEA artifact/executable, Node source, Temporal, and Rust 1.86 authorities. Rooted Windows fflate ZIPs are byte-preflighted and extracted without tar, and bind canonical unsigned metadata to real PE certificate-table evidence. macOS ditto ZIPs retain strict path/link/duplicate validation and exact Apple publisher, package payload, notarization, and benchmark bindings.",
    "risks": [
      "The final platform candidates still need to exercise target-only codesign, pkgutil, Gatekeeper, PE, Mach-O, and runtime checks after workflow integration.",
      "The deliberately strict ZIP policy accepts only flags 0 or signed-descriptor flag 0x8, ordinary stored/deflated members, and macOS ditto's exact 0x5855 timestamp/uid field sizes; it rejects every other extra-field semantic, ZIP64, non-ASCII paths, links, duplicate or overlapping members, and archives expanding beyond 2 GiB."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Wire this gate into each platform build/signing job before artifact transport or publication and upload its canonical JSON plus SHA-256 sidecar.",
      "Make every archive ship both SEA build manifests, the complete licenses directory, and internal SHA256SUMS.",
      "Pass the signed macOS PKG and benchmark sidecars into acceptance and retain each canonical acceptance receipt as a release asset."
    ]
  }
}
